Original commit body from 1d342ec:

Experiment 13.1 revealed 3 structural issues with README extraction:

1. Case-sensitive README finding missed repos using `Readme.md` (e.g., Express)
   - Fix: Use iterdir() with case-insensitive matching, prioritize by extension

2. Link reference definitions matched probes (e.g., Hugo's `[bep]: https://...`)
   - Fix: Filter lines matching `[...]: https://...` pattern

3. GitHub callout syntax matched probes (e.g., Lodash's `> [!IMPORTANT]`)
   - Fix: Filter lines matching `> [!NOTE]`, `> [!IMPORTANT]`, etc.

Results: Effective extraction rate improved from 60% to 80% on 10 diverse repos.
